      "content": "I'm truly sorry to hear that you feel so misunderstood. It's important to have someone who fully understands you and respects your perspective. Groups, counselors, or therapists who specialize in existential feelings, or those that promote authenticity and non-traditional therapy approaches, might resonate more with you. Every person is looking for meaning, and your desire to understand and even escape the \"charade\" is valid. Find a safe space where you can be heard and respected, even if that space isn't a traditional therapy setting.",
